{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 60,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The private space race has been on for a while now."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2400,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The attention has been on Space-X and Blue Origin with their reusable rockets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7029,
    "dDurationMs": 4069,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there's one private space program that's been doing things a little differently."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11800,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Richard Branson's Virgin Galactic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14230,
    "dDurationMs": 3799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "isn't building rockets at all – it's building spaceships."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23949,
    "dDurationMs": 3260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Amid the loud rivalry between Elon Musk \u0026 Jeff Bezos,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27910,
    "dDurationMs": 3859,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "amid the extravagance of self-landing rockets, and other displays,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32619,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Virgin Galactic achieved something that no other private space company ever has."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38110,
    "dDurationMs": 6049,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 2014 it became the first to put an actual person in space on board its SpaceShipOne,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44620,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "turning its pilot into an astronaut. And then on February 22nd 2019,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50920,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the VSS Unity reached space in a sub-orbital flight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55090,
    "dDurationMs": 4510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "carrying the first-ever passenger-astronaut on a private spacecraft."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59600,
    "dDurationMs": 2349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The attention of space nerds everywhere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62260,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "long distracted by the self-landing rocket club, suddenly turned back to Virgin Galactic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68049,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Questions abound! Is there a future in these strange air-launch spaceships?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73689,
    "dDurationMs": 3230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why is Richard Branson building spaceships at all?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76920,
    "dDurationMs": 6419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what other mad schemes lie in the future. And most importantly, when can WE go up?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84130,
    "dDurationMs": 3739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Obviously, these are questions probably best answered by Richard Branson."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88420,
    "dDurationMs": 7400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now in classic eccentric billionaire style, Branson spends much of his time on his private island in the British Virgin Islands."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96490,
    "dDurationMs": 2690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But my strange chance, through a series of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99970,
    "dDurationMs": 2899,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unusual events, I found myself on that island."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103270,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a long story for another time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105460,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I took the opportunity to sit Sir Richard down and blast him with questions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111200,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was all a little impromptu, so please bear with the audio."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115580,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, congratulations are in order."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117780,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "VSS Unity, SpaceShipTwo,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120440,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "successfully kissed space"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123380,
    "dDurationMs": 1739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "December 13th."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125119,
    "dDurationMs": 5479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That, that's really incredibly exciting, a huge milestone in a very long project."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132160,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[RICHARD] Yeah, thank you. It was not only exciting it was quite a relief."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137000,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, it has been 14 years of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140440,
    "dDurationMs": 6700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tears and joy. and it was just fantastic that two wonderful now-astronauts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147140,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "managed to get into space. And we've got another test flight just coming up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151800,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then we've a couple more test flights. Then we'll move the whole operation to New Mexico where we've got this beautiful spaceport"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159240,
    "dDurationMs": 6540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm hoping to go up in July. And then have many others who've signed up can go up in the years to come."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165840,
    "dDurationMs": 6900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[MATT] Well, I would say that's brave of you for proving the reliability by going up yourself before sending other people up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173240,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I have a feeling you wouldn't miss it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176330,
    "dDurationMs": 6229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[RICHARD] The reason we built a spaceship and a spaceship company was because I wanted to go up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182980,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[MATT] OK, wanting to go to space is a pretty good reason to build a spaceship."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187100,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Richard followed up with what sounds closer to his true motivation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192120,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[RICHARD] Everybody I know who's been into space who said it was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196700,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "earth changing, to be able to be in space looking back on it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201400,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's a lovely book called The Overview Effect which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203400,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is infused with all these people who've been into space. And also, space I think can do a lot to protect the Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209940,
    "dDurationMs": 1820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're also going to be putting up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211760,
    "dDurationMs": 6620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "big arrays of satellites around the world to connect people who are not connected.  And those satellites could check out on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218600,
    "dDurationMs": 5569,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "illegal fishing boats that are ravaging the ocean.  We can start monitoring the reefs in a systematic way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224420,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's an awful lot of good that has already come out of space and will come out in the years to come."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229740,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[MATT] This is a stark difference to the motivations of Musk \u0026 Bezos, who have talked many times about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235860,
    "dDurationMs": 5180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the importance of an interplanetary humanity – they want to colonize the worlds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241960,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Branson, it seems, wants to save this one. Well that sounds noble"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247140,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but if you've been following Virgin Galactic at all, you'll know that its business model is to sell tickets for rides into space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254960,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your first strategy though has been space tourism."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258700,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Can you say something about why"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260880,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where this is clearly the first"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262980,
    "dDurationMs": 660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "kind of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263980,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "commercial approach in your mind?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266400,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[RICHARD] There's only been since the Space Shuttle began"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270420,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about 500 people who are astronauts who've had the chance to go to space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276210,
    "dDurationMs": 3179,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We believe that if we can get the price at the right level, that there are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279460,
    "dDurationMs": 2780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thousands \u0026 thousands of people would love to become astronauts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282240,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I think that can,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284740,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if we if we're right about that, we can build more and more spaceships."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287140,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that means we can"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289960,
    "dDurationMs": 7560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we hope we can generate funds where we can then start thinking about point-to-point travel at great speeds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297740,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And overriding all of this, both space and point-to-point travel and satellites in space, is a desire to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304960,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bring the environmental"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307080,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "effect down to an absolute minimum. So we can put somebody into space"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311640,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for about the same environmental effect of sending somebody, one person, on a plane from London to New York and back. And because we're"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319400,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "air-launching our rockets to put satellites into space,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322660,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's much more environmentally friendly than a big giant rocket on the ground going to space"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328000,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[MATT] It's very exciting. Space planes are intrinsically"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331319,
    "dDurationMs": 4459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more science-fictiony than rockets. And I think they're inspiring in that sense."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335840,
    "dDurationMs": 5140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I love these images of SpaceShipOne and SpaceShipTwo dropping off and flying up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342300,
    "dDurationMs": 1220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[RICHARD] I think somehow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343520,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you're going to go into space you should be on a spaceship."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346220,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[MATT] Let's take a look at what humanity's first private spacecraft looks like, and why it might be the solution to affordable space access."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354029,
    "dDurationMs": 5330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the VSS Unity on its second trip to space on February 22nd."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 359600,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unity is dropped at 15,000 meters by its carrier, White Night, after which it blasts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364920,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's rocket engine sending it into a sub-orbital flight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368760,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unity's first two space flights took it to around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 372000,
    "dDurationMs": 7800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "83 and 90 kilometers respectively. For reference 80 kilometers above sea level is the boundary of space used by the U.S."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380039,
    "dDurationMs": 5899,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is still below the 100 kilometer Karman Line, an alternate definition to the space boundary."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386339,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Unity is designed to hit a 110 kilometers in standard operations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392639,
    "dDurationMs": 6500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After a few minutes in space the craft re-enters and lands. It never reaches orbital velocity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399269,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it's low speed reentry is less fraught than say the space shuttle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405269,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unity is actually the second of the SpaceShipTwo class space planes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408980,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first, Enterprise, was lost along with one of its pilots in a tragic crash in 2014."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 415280,
    "dDurationMs": 8480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The previous generation, SpaceShipOne, was actually the first private piloted craft to cross the Karman Line in 2004"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424280,
    "dDurationMs": 7780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is some incredible engineering genius behind this craft, most of which is thanks to aerospace engineer Burt Rutan."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432689,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the key innovation is the whole air-launch thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436709,
    "dDurationMs": 6350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's worth a quick word on. Obviously the space plane itself needs less fuel than a craft launched from the ground."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 443420,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But why is air-launching from a plane more efficient than using booster rockets?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 448520,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the real key is that planes are more efficient than rockets at low altitude. As well as a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455279,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "combustible fuel as an energy source,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457589,
    "dDurationMs": 7660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rockets need to carry an oxidant to burn that fuel and a reaction mass – that's what you blast out to propel the rocket forward."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465830,
    "dDurationMs": 4789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Planes, on the other hand, can use air as both oxidant and reaction mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471080,
    "dDurationMs": 5539,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They only need to carry the energy supply which is usually a combustible fuel, but could also"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477290,
    "dDurationMs": 5089,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "eventually be electricity.  In addition, an air-launch craft can be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482690,
    "dDurationMs": 2660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "optimized for the low pressure of that altitude,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 485900,
    "dDurationMs": 2779,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rather than have to operate at a range of pressures."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489680,
    "dDurationMs": 4789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whether air launch can beat out reusable rockets for actually putting things into orbit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495020,
    "dDurationMs": 6829,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "remains to be seen. But the technique is looking great for sub-orbital travel. And this is what Richard means when he says"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 502250,
    "dDurationMs": 7790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "point-to-point travel. These space-kissing trajectories could one day allow us to travel halfway across the globe in a couple of hours."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510320,
    "dDurationMs": 6650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Perhaps in the future everyone who travels overseas will also become an astronaut. But I'm less patient than that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517160,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When do WE get to go to space?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 520020,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are 500 past astronauts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522160,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You already have a couple of hundred more than that signed up to fly to space with Virgin Galactic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528970,
    "dDurationMs": 4019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you're going to more than double the number of astronauts that there were, in short order."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533900,
    "dDurationMs": 3229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's a price tag, a quarter million dollar per ticket."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537980,
    "dDurationMs": 5020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do you see this as something that the average person is going to be able to do?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543000,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[RICHARD] Yeah, I think"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 544580,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you compare it to commercial aviation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547660,
    "dDurationMs": 7640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to cross the Atlantic in the 20s cost roughly the equivalent of a quarter million dollars today. Over the hundred years since"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 555830,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the price has come down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 557480,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if we're right in believing that a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561940,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spaceship company is going"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564120,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be successful and we can attract people who are willing to pay"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568180,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the quarter of a million dollars that we currently charge, then"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572260,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can start building more and more spaceships. And as you build more spaceships the price can start coming down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 577680,
    "dDurationMs": 4789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So 25 years from now, I hope that a lot of young people watching"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 582470,
    "dDurationMs": 5970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this program will be able to afford to go to space and will become astronauts then."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 588440,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's a very exciting thing for them to look forward to."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591980,
    "dDurationMs": 560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[MATT] So there you have it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 592709,
    "dDurationMs": 7760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe 25 years, earlier if you get rich. Richard Branson is 68 and has been waiting a long time for this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600779,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I guess we can hold out a bit longer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603899,
    "dDurationMs": 5900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, so we have sub-orbital joyrides and saving the world by improving our access to space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610440,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what about the far future?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 612960,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Richard shared a pretty unique vision with us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 616120,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[RICHARD] You know, my dream will be to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618740,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "let me start the Virgin Hotel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 621000,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Either just off the Moon or on the Moon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 624080,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No slightly just off the Moon. People who stay at our hotel will be able to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630320,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will have these lovely glass pods where they can see the Moon clearly from their pods."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635140,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then we can have little spaceships that can"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 638120,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whisk them around the moon and back in the evenings for dinner."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641740,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[MATT] You've got these beautiful electric buggies here on the islands,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 645480,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they're fun.  These would be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648200,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[RICHARD] Yeah, so you can program it just to go a few hundred feet above the Moon's surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652500,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I love to dream. In the years to come,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 655460,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "either ourselves or Elon or Jeff Bezos,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 659640,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we will be looking at a deeper and deeper space exploration. But in order to afford that we need"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667340,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thousands of people to be able to sign up to go into space. And then use the resources to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672740,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "expand into deeper space exploration."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677320,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[MATT] Sir Richard, thank you the talking to us, but thank you mostly for dreaming for us, and with us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 683680,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It could be a very exciting future."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686080,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[RICHARD] It will be a very exciting future. And thank you for inspiring us with your knowledge, it's fantastic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 692000,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He's the only person who calls me \"Sir Richard\" nobody else calls me \"Sir Richard\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695840,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I heard it once before when I was walking down a New York street."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700320,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I thought it was a Shakespearean play taking place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703260,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[MATT] I don't meet enough Knights.  I'm going to call him Sir Richard."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 706500,
    "dDurationMs": 1180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[RICHARD] Cheers, thanks so much.\n[MATT] Thank you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 707940,
    "dDurationMs": 6680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[MATT] SIR Richard Branson's long quest to send himself, and before too long many of the rest of us into space, is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 714900,
    "dDurationMs": 2629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reaching its fruition, with lofty goals ahead."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 718560,
    "dDurationMs": 6349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Branson has said that he'll go up in July.  And while the first paying passengers aren't yet scheduled,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 725250,
    "dDurationMs": 3289,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "presumably they'll follow when it's as safe as these things can be."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728970,
    "dDurationMs": 4309,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, Elon Musk is hot on Richard Branson's heels. On March 2nd"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 733740,
    "dDurationMs": 6410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "SpaceX's Dragon 2 spacecraft made its first successful trip to space, and not on a sub-orbital trajectory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 740520,
    "dDurationMs": 2209,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It actually docked with the International Space Station."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743400,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the first private spacecraft"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 745589,
    "dDurationMs": 6380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "designed to carry humans to make it into true orbit. Now Dragon 2 didn't have passengers on this test,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752190,
    "dDurationMs": 4669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but in July it will.  The private space race is heating up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 757500,
    "dDurationMs": 7849,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a hell of a time to be alive, watching humanity's first tentative steps off the Earth, and into the fringes of space time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766080,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey everyone, before we get to comments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768080,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I want to let you know about the new PBS Digital Studios show, Sound Field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772960,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sound Field is a music show that gives a complete breakdown of songs and artists in every genre"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778060,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from pop, classical, rap, jazz, electronic, country, rock, and more. And this week"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 783589,
    "dDurationMs": 7590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they have a very mathy episode on the Fibonacci Sequence and Golden Ratio in music and how its influenced"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 791480,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "everyone from Bela Bartok to Queen to Drake."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 794860,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Alright, last week we explored the bad science of perpetual motion machines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 799480,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and announced the winners of the perpetual motion challenge. Check them out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 803600,
    "dDurationMs": 1390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their brilliant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804990,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, let's see what you had to say."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 807600,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "HitAndMissLab points out that atoms are perpetual motion machines,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 811680,
    "dDurationMs": 4099,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and there are hydrogen atoms that have been ticking for the entire age of the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 816720,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, I guess you could call the atom the best possible perpetual motion machine of the Third Kind."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824320,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The type that can keep on ticking without energy input or output."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828060,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But even these eventually fail."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 831420,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Electrons escape their orbits by quantum tunneling, and protons themselves may eventually decay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 838100,
    "dDurationMs": 7100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mark Segal and Pieces'O'Cake Maleck asked what if the cog part of the Brownian ratchet is in a vacuum?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845730,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now to remind you, the Brownian ratchet has this flywheel that turns a cog"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 850700,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "due to random motions of particles hitting the flywheel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854480,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there's a latch that allows the cog to turn only in one direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 858320,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the cog half of the device is at the same temperature or higher,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 862940,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It can be shown that it's just as likely to turn backwards as forwards when the latch raises."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 868520,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, what if the cog is in a vacuum, so there are no particles to turn it backwards?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 873500,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the cog itself is made of particles that vibrate thermally."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 878780,
    "dDurationMs": 7560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A device light enough to rotate its flywheel due to being hit by individual particles will also have a lot of internal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 886460,
    "dDurationMs": 6860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thermal vibration. Even in a vacuum, that internal vibration is enough to randomize its rotational motion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 894000,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In short, nature will always find a way to ruin our free lunch."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 898800,
    "dDurationMs": 5900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A few of you chastised us for putting the ElectroBOOM video that debunks perpetual motion machines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 905160,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "alongside all of the other videos that actually claim to have built one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 909960,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So yeah, we put a shout-out to ElectroBOOM's channel in text."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 914500,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we thought that that text made it clear that we think he's a genius, and you should all watch his videos."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920960,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Apparently that text wasn't clear enough. So let me say it again:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 924990,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Go watch ElectrOBOOM."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 926880,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A couple of you referenced Ginsberg's Theorem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 929860,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Allen Ginsberg's interpretation of the three laws of thermodynamics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 934540,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It goes like this:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 936070,
    "dDurationMs": 2630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Law 1: you can't win."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 938700,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Law 2: you can't break even."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 941460,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And Law 3: You can't stop playing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 944580,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can't get energy from nothing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 947760,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You'll always lose energy as entropy increases. And you can never not have some entropy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 954200,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, you can never beat the house."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 956920,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But remember, the house is the entire universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 960880,
    "dDurationMs": 6840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can still win individual hands now and then at the expense of other players. Like by stealing their aces"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 967860,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "aka energy, and giving them your 2's aka entropy, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 973140,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, this is where we leave particle gambling metaphors to the great poets."
    } ]
  } ]
}
